# Virtual pads and the uaccess tag (06-input.md section 3, rule 3; RUY-446).
# 70-ruya-input.rules leaves the virtual pads (phys ruya-input/pad<n>) untagged, but systemd's
# 70-uaccess.rules sorts after it and tags every joystick, a virtual pad included. That made logind give
# the seat's user, ruya-shell, an ACL entry on the node. This file sorts after 70-uaccess.rules and
# before 73-seat-late.rules (which applies the ACL), so the tag is gone when logind looks. Keyboards and
# mice (ruya-input/kbm*) are not matched: they keep uaccess, the shell's libinput reads them.
SUBSYSTEM!="input", GOTO="ruya_input_pad_end"
KERNEL!="event*", GOTO="ruya_input_pad_end"
ATTRS{phys}=="ruya-input/pad*", TAG-="uaccess", OWNER="ruya-input", MODE="0600"
LABEL="ruya_input_pad_end"
